1.e4 {Notes by C. Von Bardeleben.} e6 2.d4 d5 3.exd5 exd5
4.Nf3 Nf6 5.Bd3 Bd6 6.O-O O-O 7.Nc3 c6 8.Ne2 Nbd7 9.Ng3 Re8
10.Nf5 Bc7 11.Bg5 {I prefer 11 Nf3h4 Nf8 12 Qf3.} Nf8 12.Qd2
Bxf5 13.Bxf5 Qd6 {! By this move Black obtains an attack.}
14.Bh4 Ne4 15.Qd3 g6 16.Bh3 f5 17.Bg3 f4 18.Bh4 h6 19.Ne5 Bb6
{If ...g5 white answers 20 f3.} 20.Kh1 {White cannot avoid
material loss. Bad would be 20 c3 because of ...g5 21 f3 gxh4
22 fxe4 Qxe5 winning a piece.} Bxd4 {! Now ...g5 would be
inefficacious on account of 21 f3.} 21.Nxc6 Bg7 22.Ne7+ {White
cannot save the piece for if he plays 22 Na5 there follows
Nc5! 23 Qf3 g5 24 Rad1 Ne4 25 Nxb7 Qc6 26 Na5 Qb5 and black
wins a piece.} Rxe7 23.Bxe7 Qxe7 24.Qxd5+ Kh7 25.f3 Ng5 {Black
should have played ...Nf6 26 Qb3 Re8 or 26 Qd2 Rd8 27 Qf2 Qb4
28 c3 Qc4 again ...Ng5 is not good because White with his
following move occupies the king's file.} 26.Rae1 Qc7 27.Re2
Rd8 28.Qb3 Nxh3 29.gxh3 Rd6 30.Rfe1 Rd7 31.Re8 Qd6 32.c4 Qf6
33.c5 Qh4 {...Qc6 was much better.} 34.Qb4 Rf7 35.Qb3 Qf6
36.Qd5 g5 37.b4 Ng6 38.b5 Qf5 39.Qxf5 Rxf5 40.Rc1 Bb2 {Black
ought to have played ...Rf7 instead; 41 Rc8 Be5 42 c6 bxc6 43
bxc6 Ne7 44 Ra8 Nd5.} 41.Rc2 Bd4 42.Rd2 Bxc5 {Disastrous; the
best move was ...Bg7.} 43.Rd7+ Ne7 44.Rexe7+ Kg6 45.Re6+ Kh5
46.Rh7 Bf8 47.a4 Rd5 48.Rf6 Rd8 49.Kg2 b6 50.Kf1 Re8 51.Rh8
Bg7 52.Rfxh6+ Bxh6 53.Rxe8 1-0